※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4623 LANG_CONTAINER_CANNOT_COPY

※ A sum holding text is copied into a container part by part, but an array of
※ text it holds is not yet: an array held inside something else is its elements
※ where the something is, and the copy of one would be a walk of its own.  So a
※ sum holding one, made in an arena the list does not outlast, cannot go in
※ (4623) -- which is what holds of a record holding one, too.

type Cell = names : str⟦2⟧ | none : void

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let held: mut [Cell] = []
    foreach i := 0u32…2u32:
        let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
        let made: str = "a" ⧺ ⍕i in pool
        let c: Cell = Cell(.names ← ⟦made, "c"⟧ in pool)
        held ⧺← [c]
    if #held = 2: 0u6 else: 1u6
